1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:26,520
Welcome, thanks so much for joining us, whether you're here in person or watching online.

2
00:00:26,520 --> 00:00:28,160
If you don't know me, my name is Ryan.

3
00:00:28,260 --> 00:00:30,520
I have the privilege of being one of the pastors here at Canvas.

4
00:00:30,520 --> 00:00:33,720
Super excited to continue our series through the book of James.

5
00:00:33,720 --> 00:00:37,480
You might have noticed on your way in that the communion cups are not out like normal.

6
00:00:37,480 --> 00:00:40,320
We regularly try and take communion every single week.

7
00:00:40,320 --> 00:00:50,260
And this week, our plan is at the end of service just to spend some time intentionally and on purpose praying for the nation of Ukraine in light of that.

8
00:00:50,260 --> 00:00:57,480
You know, part of communion is about remembering Jesus, but it's also about bringing us around the table that we've all been invited to as a family of God.

9
00:00:57,480 --> 00:01:04,560
And there are believers all over the nation of Ukraine that probably would love to be able to take communion this morning and aren't going to be able to.

10
00:01:04,560 --> 00:01:08,440
And so we just want to take some time to just honor them.

11
00:01:08,440 --> 00:01:13,380
And, you know, Scripture says to rejoice with those who rejoice and to weep with those who weep.

12
00:01:13,620 --> 00:01:22,160
And, you know, we just live in a culture where it's really easy to get focused on just our circles of influence and the things around us.

13
00:01:22,160 --> 00:01:30,300
And so, you know, we're part not only of a big C church in our city, big C church in our country, but big C church around the world.

14
00:01:30,300 --> 00:01:33,640
And so we definitely want to take some time to do that.

15
00:01:33,640 --> 00:01:40,800
And also excited about that service in a couple of weeks just to come together with other churches and to practically say, like, it's not about turf wars.

16
00:01:40,800 --> 00:01:46,640
It's not about what brand we have in our city, what our website is, what our logo is.

17
00:01:46,640 --> 00:01:50,220
But it's about Jesus Christ and building his church and building his kingdom.

18
00:01:50,220 --> 00:01:51,140
We say this all the time.

19
00:01:51,140 --> 00:01:58,860
One of my favorite things about Canvas is we say that we want to see the kingdom of God built in the city of Winchester as it is in heaven.

20
00:01:58,860 --> 00:02:05,940
And that's really one of our core values here at Canvas is to be a kingdom-focused church.

21
00:02:06,340 --> 00:02:07,800
And that's not just something that we say.

22
00:02:07,800 --> 00:02:11,160
It's something that we want to see manifested in our city.

23
00:02:11,160 --> 00:02:24,080
So I'd also, again, just to kind of rehash some of the announcements, I'd love to invite you to be a part of that group just to pray for what might be next for our church and to kind of contribute to that.

24
00:02:24,080 --> 00:02:26,960
I get questions all the time about what I think, what people think.

25
00:02:26,960 --> 00:02:30,340
People want to know what I think the next chapter of our church is going to look like.

26
00:02:30,340 --> 00:02:32,160
And what I've been saying is I have no clue.

27
00:02:32,840 --> 00:02:41,000
But what I do know is that I'm convinced beyond a shadow of a doubt that there is a community of people here that I want to build the kingdom of God with.

28
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:55,120
Whatever that looks like, whatever kind of forms that might take over the next couple of months or even years, I know that there are people here that are real people with real lives who want to see the kingdom of God built in our city.

29
00:02:55,120 --> 00:02:57,440
And as long as we have that, we've got a church.

30
00:02:57,440 --> 00:02:58,320
That's all I know.

31
00:02:59,640 --> 00:03:04,380
So we're going to continue our series through the book of James.

32
00:03:04,380 --> 00:03:11,360
I made a joke a couple of weeks ago that I didn't want to be the guy that was going to preach through a book of the Bible for like a year.

33
00:03:11,360 --> 00:03:13,280
Not that there's anything wrong with those guys.

34
00:03:13,280 --> 00:03:14,360
I listen to those guys.

35
00:03:14,360 --> 00:03:15,940
I find value from those guys.

36
00:03:15,940 --> 00:03:17,240
It's just not me.

37
00:03:17,240 --> 00:03:18,360
I didn't want to be that guy.

38
00:03:18,360 --> 00:03:22,340
And then God just keeps making me do things I don't want to do.

39
00:03:22,340 --> 00:03:25,680
I'm going to go backwards in the book of James this week.

40
00:03:25,680 --> 00:03:29,180
We're going to spend some time in a text that we already went through.

41
00:03:29,180 --> 00:03:32,760
We're going to go forward too, but we're going to go backwards so that we can go forward.

42
00:03:32,760 --> 00:03:36,000
So if you have your Bibles, I'd love to have you open up to the book of James.

43
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:47,680
And the reason that I'm going to go backwards in order to go forwards is because the passage that we're going to get to this morning really is a hinge passage for the rest of the book of James.

44
00:03:47,920 --> 00:03:54,600
So it's really important that we understand this passage because it's going to set us up for the rest of James' teachings.

45
00:03:54,600 --> 00:03:58,800
Because James has, like I said at the beginning of this series, James has some really practical teachings.

46
00:03:58,800 --> 00:04:18,280
And if we're not careful, if we don't understand how he's setting those practical teachings up, if we don't understand the foundation that he's laying for those practical teachings, it would be really easy for us to get kind of trapped in this moral concept where we just think he's addressing moral behaviors rather than heart conditions.

47
00:04:18,280 --> 00:04:27,280
Which what he's going to do this morning is he's going to set us up that behavior, what we think about when we think about moral behavior and whether we're being obedient to God's word or not.

48
00:04:27,460 --> 00:04:31,940
What matters is our heart condition, not the external behaviors.

49
00:04:31,940 --> 00:04:37,340
And so if we don't understand that, we can get trapped in this, like, moral, religious behavior modification.

50
00:04:37,340 --> 00:04:39,460
And that's not what the book of James is about.

51
00:04:39,460 --> 00:04:48,640
The book of James is expounding on the teachings of Jesus and what it looks like to follow Jesus first from our hearts and then externally it produces fruit.

52
00:04:48,640 --> 00:04:50,260
So hopefully that makes sense.

53
00:04:50,260 --> 00:04:52,880
It might seem like I'm beating a dead horse today.

54
00:04:52,980 --> 00:04:56,900
As I was kind of thinking through my notes, I'm like, man, I'm really hammering home on this one point.

55
00:04:56,900 --> 00:05:00,900
But I think it's going to set us up for the rest of the book of James.

56
00:05:00,900 --> 00:05:01,420
Does that make sense?

57
00:05:01,420 --> 00:05:03,320
Thanks, Corey.

58
00:05:03,320 --> 00:05:08,740
Let me pray and then we'll hop in.

59
00:05:08,740 --> 00:05:14,620
Father, we thank you so much for this opportunity that we have to gather together with other believers,

60
00:05:14,620 --> 00:05:22,440
the freedom that we have to do so and the location that we have to do so and just the resources that you provide for us.

61
00:05:22,500 --> 00:05:24,120
Yeah, we're still us and we don't realize it.

62
00:05:24,120 --> 00:05:25,800
We look over it all the time.

63
00:05:25,800 --> 00:05:27,260
I look over it all the time.

64
00:05:27,260 --> 00:05:30,700
And so, Holy Spirit, I just pray that you'd be present in this room.

65
00:05:30,700 --> 00:05:37,600
As you are present in rooms all across the city of Winchester, all across our country, and all across the world this morning,

66
00:05:37,600 --> 00:05:47,440
as you are sharing with each individual believer what they need to hear to better follow Jesus, to better apprentice with Jesus.

67
00:05:47,820 --> 00:05:51,240
So, God, I just pray for whatever happens in this room.

68
00:05:51,240 --> 00:05:52,280
I pray that it would be of you.

69
00:05:52,280 --> 00:05:55,780
God, that you would get me out of the way, that you would get our worship team out of the way,

70
00:05:55,780 --> 00:06:00,420
that you would increase and we would decrease for your glory, for our good.

71
00:06:00,420 --> 00:06:02,160
In Jesus' name I pray.

72
00:06:02,160 --> 00:06:02,880
Amen.

73
00:06:03,440 --> 00:06:06,080
I'm going to be in the ESV this morning.

74
00:06:06,080 --> 00:06:13,780
I normally am in the NLC, so if you've got a Bible app and you want to follow Word for Word, it should be in the ESV or it should be on the screen behind us.

75
00:06:13,780 --> 00:06:18,580
As we get ready to hop into James chapter 1, I'd love to get some participation like normal.

76
00:06:18,680 --> 00:06:22,600
How many of you in this room would consider yourself a bargain shopper?

77
00:06:22,600 --> 00:06:26,680
We've got bargain shoppers and we've got generic people in the room.

78
00:06:26,680 --> 00:06:30,820
We've got any Kirkland Signature Warriors in here.

79
00:06:30,820 --> 00:06:33,380
No judgment to our fancy people.

80
00:06:33,380 --> 00:06:39,760
We have, for those of you online, you know, 80% of our people are bargain shoppers, but no judgment to the rest of you.

81
00:06:40,660 --> 00:06:45,580
I tend to prefer generic things except for when it comes to clothing.

82
00:06:45,580 --> 00:07:00,480
And not because I'm a fashionista or because I'm good at style, but for whatever reason, clothes are the one thing that I tend to be able to notice quality differences when it comes to generic versus not generic.

83
00:07:00,480 --> 00:07:10,540
And the best illustration that I have for this is, like, I'm a classic middle-aged white man, and so when fall comes around, I put on flannels.

84
00:07:10,660 --> 00:07:12,460
You know, I have flannels, I put them on.

85
00:07:12,460 --> 00:07:17,260
And I've got some flannels from Old Navy, and I've got a couple of L.L. Bean flannels.

86
00:07:17,260 --> 00:07:20,340
And they look very similar on the outside.

87
00:07:20,340 --> 00:07:28,800
Like, if you just saw me walk into the room, you'd be like, eh, like, you probably wouldn't be able to tell from 20 or 30 feet which are the Old Navy flannels or which are the L.L. Bean flannels.

88
00:07:28,800 --> 00:07:33,560
But if you wash the Old Navy flannels, like, five times, that's it.

89
00:07:33,560 --> 00:07:34,080
You're done.

90
00:07:34,080 --> 00:07:35,000
They're gone.

91
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:37,120
Like, they are, they're no longer.

92
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:45,640
But I've got, I've got L.L. Bean flannels that are probably going to be around when I'm no longer around because those things are just different, right?

93
00:07:45,640 --> 00:07:52,800
Like, they look similar on the outside, but when it comes to quality, when it comes to substance, like, they're totally different.

94
00:07:52,800 --> 00:07:59,880
And if you're not tracking with the fashionista illustration, if you're like, what are we doing here, I'll transition to a different illustration.

95
00:07:59,880 --> 00:08:01,680
So let's think about houses.

96
00:08:02,640 --> 00:08:07,300
I've owned three houses at this point, which is way too many for a 30-year-old person to have owned.

97
00:08:07,300 --> 00:08:12,560
I, you know, ministry sometimes makes you play ping-pong geographically.

98
00:08:12,560 --> 00:08:20,960
But the first house that I owned was in Inwood, and it was one of those, like, new-built, Dan Ryan fast houses, right?

99
00:08:20,960 --> 00:08:24,540
The second house I owned was in Wilkes-Barre, a coal mining town.

100
00:08:24,540 --> 00:08:26,740
And so that house was built in, like, the 20s.

101
00:08:27,140 --> 00:08:31,780
And from the outside, looking at it from the outside, the houses look pretty similar.

102
00:08:31,780 --> 00:08:34,660
You wouldn't really have a whole lot of difference.

103
00:08:34,660 --> 00:08:41,440
But when you go into the attic, the attic of my Inwood house looked like it was built with toothpicks and, like, glue, right?

104
00:08:41,440 --> 00:08:44,160
And I'm just, like, I'm, like, looking at this thing, and I'm like, huh.

105
00:08:44,160 --> 00:08:46,520
Did I make a good purchase?

106
00:08:46,520 --> 00:08:49,260
Luckily, the market was hot, so I resold it.

107
00:08:49,260 --> 00:08:49,660
We're good.

108
00:08:49,660 --> 00:08:54,400
But you walk into that attic in Wilkes-Barre in, like, timbers, like beams, right?

109
00:08:54,400 --> 00:08:56,260
Like, real, solid wood.

110
00:08:56,260 --> 00:08:58,400
That house was built right.

111
00:08:58,400 --> 00:09:01,680
And on the outside, they looked very similar.

112
00:09:01,680 --> 00:09:05,980
But the quality is so much different.

113
00:09:05,980 --> 00:09:11,360
And the reason I open up with this illustration is because I believe James is really trying to get us to understand

114
00:09:11,360 --> 00:09:15,900
that there's really two versions of following Jesus.

115
00:09:15,900 --> 00:09:20,940
There's two versions of Christianity that, from the outside, look very similar.

116
00:09:22,420 --> 00:09:32,460
But when, upon further inspection, upon trials and temptations, as he talked about previously, upon difficulty arising, the quality is much different.

117
00:09:32,460 --> 00:09:43,700
So I think what James is going to say here this morning is he's going to say, don't be deceived into moral living when you've been invited into spiritual flourishing.

118
00:09:43,700 --> 00:09:53,460
Like, these are these two versions of Christianity that, on the outside, look very similar, but upon further inspection, they're totally different.

119
00:09:53,460 --> 00:10:06,700
Moral living, like, behavior modification, like, just checking a few boxes, doing a few of the right things, just becoming a little bit better of a person, it looks really similar to spiritual flourishing.

120
00:10:06,800 --> 00:10:16,840
It looks really similar to transformation from the inside out on the outside, like, if you just interact with people who are religious versus people who are literally being transformed from the inside out,

121
00:10:16,840 --> 00:10:19,240
you're not going to see a whole lot of difference on the surface.

122
00:10:19,240 --> 00:10:31,400
But when trials and temptations come, when difficulty comes, like, when real life happens, you want to be the person that's building your life from the inside out, not from the outside in.

123
00:10:31,460 --> 00:10:41,180
But if we're not careful, if we don't get what James is saying here, it can be really easy for us to be tempted to just focus on the outside in rather than inside out.

124
00:10:41,180 --> 00:10:52,660
So James is going to say, as we continue through this book, as we talk about external behaviors, I want you to focus on those behaviors coming from the inside out and not from the outside.

125
00:10:53,800 --> 00:11:00,360
And I think, if we're being honest, many of us that have grown up in the church that might have religious backgrounds, we're not careful.

126
00:11:00,360 --> 00:11:06,020
It could be really easy for us to slide into focusing on external things rather than internal things.

127
00:11:06,020 --> 00:11:11,760
It could be really easy for us to focus on behavior modification rather than spiritual transformation.

128
00:11:11,760 --> 00:11:23,220
And honestly, there might be some of you in this room that would say, I've never even really given Christianity a fair shot because I don't really care about the moral behavior modification.

129
00:11:23,420 --> 00:11:28,360
Like, you've been taught that that's the message of Jesus, that the message of Jesus is just come and be obedient.

130
00:11:28,360 --> 00:11:36,620
When in reality, the message of Jesus is come, follow me, I will give you abundant life, spiritual flourishing.

131
00:11:36,620 --> 00:11:42,740
And so James is going to say, look, there's two types of, and he's talking to religious people, right?

132
00:11:42,740 --> 00:11:53,400
He's talking to Jewish believers, and it would be really easy for them to slide back away from the word of truth, the message of the gospel, back into do this, don't do this.

133
00:11:53,420 --> 00:11:55,200
Just do this, don't do this.

134
00:11:55,200 --> 00:12:01,800
So James is going to say, hey, don't be deceived into moral living when you've been invited to spiritual flourishing.

135
00:12:01,800 --> 00:12:03,640
Morality leads to hypocrisy.

136
00:12:03,640 --> 00:12:05,060
It leads to anger.

137
00:12:05,060 --> 00:12:05,740
It leads to bitterness.

138
00:12:05,740 --> 00:12:07,020
It leads to a hard heart.

139
00:12:07,020 --> 00:12:10,660
Spiritual flourishing leads to abundant life.

140
00:12:11,480 --> 00:12:19,740
And then at the end, he's going to give us this illustration that's going to help us decipher whether or not we're focusing on morality or spiritual flourishing.

141
00:12:19,740 --> 00:12:20,700
Does that make sense?

142
00:12:20,700 --> 00:12:24,960
It's kind of the trajectory that we're going the rest of our time here in James.

143
00:12:25,040 --> 00:12:30,300
So James 1, starting in verse 16, I told you we were going backwards, but we will go forward.

144
00:12:30,300 --> 00:12:34,980
It says, don't be deceived, my beloved brothers.

145
00:12:34,980 --> 00:12:45,620
Brothers, every good gift and every perfect gift is from above, coming down from the Father of lights, with whom there is no variation or shadow due to change.

146
00:12:45,760 --> 00:12:53,800
Of God's own will, he brought us forth by the word of truth that we should have a kind of firstfruits of his creation.

147
00:12:53,800 --> 00:12:57,260
Verse 21, he goes on and he says, therefore.

148
00:12:57,260 --> 00:13:07,660
So that therefore is kind of a hinged passage connecting us to that word of truth that we should be, that human beings should be a firstfruits of all creation.

149
00:13:07,660 --> 00:13:17,360
He says, therefore, put away all filthiness and rampant wickedness and receive with meekness the implanted word, which is able to save your souls.

150
00:13:17,360 --> 00:13:22,300
He says, be doers of the word and not hearers only, deceiving yourselves.

151
00:13:22,300 --> 00:13:29,080
There's a theme there that you can be deceived into a version of Christianity that really isn't the real thing.

152
00:13:29,080 --> 00:13:35,640
He says, for if anyone is a hearer of the word and not a doer, he is like a man who looks intently at his natural face in the mirror.

153
00:13:35,760 --> 00:13:41,180
For he looks at himself and then goes away and at once forgets what he looked like.

154
00:13:41,180 --> 00:13:53,120
But the one who looks into the perfect law, the law of liberty and perseveres, being no hearer who forgets but a doer who acts, he will be blessed in his doing.

155
00:13:53,120 --> 00:13:59,720
So James says, don't be deceived into moral living when you've been invited into spiritual flourishing.

156
00:13:59,720 --> 00:14:09,720
In verse 18, he says that there's this process of restoration, this process of reconciliation that God has begun in Jesus.

157
00:14:09,720 --> 00:14:14,780
And he says that we are the firstfruits of that process of restoration.

158
00:14:14,780 --> 00:14:22,980
Romans says that all of creation is eagerly anticipating God's reconciliation, God's restoration of all things.

159
00:14:22,980 --> 00:14:30,140
And so literally, like, the trees and the waters and the animals know that, like, earth is not as it should be.

160
00:14:30,140 --> 00:14:37,360
Like, they know that God has a plan to make all things right again, to restore everything back to his original creation.

161
00:14:37,360 --> 00:14:41,380
But it says that we are the firstfruits of that process.

162
00:14:41,380 --> 00:14:44,380
So God is in the process of making all things new again.

163
00:14:44,520 --> 00:14:47,380
And that process, crazily enough, starts with us.

164
00:14:47,380 --> 00:14:48,680
And how does it start with us?

165
00:14:48,680 --> 00:14:51,000
Does it start with us being moral people?

166
00:14:51,000 --> 00:14:53,560
Does it start with us obeying a law?

167
00:14:53,560 --> 00:15:00,720
No, it starts by the word of truth, by the proclamation of the message of the gospel.

168
00:15:00,720 --> 00:15:03,420
Jesus started this process of reconciliation.

169
00:15:03,420 --> 00:15:09,460
He has given the invitation to all of creation to submit under his lordship,

170
00:15:09,540 --> 00:15:13,340
to believe that he has done everything that was required by the law perfectly,

171
00:15:13,340 --> 00:15:16,940
that we might come under that, that we might receive that word of truth,

172
00:15:16,940 --> 00:15:20,760
that we might begin to be conformed back into the image of Jesus,

173
00:15:20,760 --> 00:15:24,200
which was what we were created for from the very beginning.

174
00:15:24,200 --> 00:15:25,600
This is spiritual flourishing.

175
00:15:25,600 --> 00:15:27,000
This is what we've been invited to.

176
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:30,820
Not behavior modification, not just changing a few of our behaviors,

177
00:15:30,820 --> 00:15:38,360
but literally receiving the word of truth and becoming more like Jesus for the rest of our lives.

178
00:15:39,200 --> 00:15:45,620
Sin has broken God's design, and he has an eternal plan to restore all things to himself.

179
00:15:45,620 --> 00:15:48,740
And that plan starts with us.

180
00:15:48,740 --> 00:15:52,680
It doesn't start with us following a long list of rules.

181
00:15:52,680 --> 00:15:56,660
It starts with us receiving the word of truth.

182
00:15:56,660 --> 00:15:59,180
And this is a pattern that we're going to see throughout this passage.

183
00:15:59,180 --> 00:16:02,220
Three times he's going to use a phrase that's very similar.

184
00:16:02,220 --> 00:16:04,940
He's going to start with receive the word of truth,

185
00:16:04,940 --> 00:16:07,920
and then he's going to call it the implanted word,

186
00:16:08,240 --> 00:16:12,420
and later he's going to call it the perfect law of liberty.

187
00:16:13,760 --> 00:16:18,900
And I think what he's doing there is he's drawing out this pattern of salvation,

188
00:16:18,900 --> 00:16:23,760
this pattern of following Jesus that really resembles the story that Jesus teaches,

189
00:16:23,760 --> 00:16:26,180
like about the parable of the sower.

190
00:16:26,180 --> 00:16:31,360
Like he's saying, the word of truth has been passed out to all of creation.

191
00:16:32,080 --> 00:16:36,980
God's word, the message of hope, the message of restoration has been given to all of creation.

192
00:16:36,980 --> 00:16:41,460
And for those of us who will receive it, it becomes an implanted word.

193
00:16:41,460 --> 00:16:46,740
Like we receive it, and it's like a seed that goes into good soil.

194
00:16:46,920 --> 00:16:53,680
And as that good soil is watered, it leads to liberty, it leads to freedom, it leads to life.

195
00:16:53,680 --> 00:16:57,700
James is saying here there's a type of following Jesus.

196
00:16:57,700 --> 00:17:02,860
There's a way to follow Jesus that starts with the inside, starts with receiving the word of truth,

197
