412
00:31:33,680 --> 00:31:41,780
Like, for those of us that read the word on a regular basis, it's really easy for you to just, like, scroll through a paragraph and check a box.

413
00:31:41,780 --> 00:31:43,820
I do that sometimes in my Bible reading plan.

414
00:31:43,820 --> 00:31:45,200
I'm just like, I just got to get through it today.

415
00:31:45,200 --> 00:31:48,540
No, like, let it speak truth into your life.

416
00:31:48,540 --> 00:31:51,400
Let it confront areas of your life that aren't like Jesus.

417
00:31:51,400 --> 00:31:52,240
Let it tell you.

418
00:31:52,240 --> 00:31:54,640
And then learn to agree with it.

419
00:31:54,740 --> 00:31:57,020
Learn to believe that God's ways are better than your ways.

420
00:31:57,020 --> 00:31:59,300
Assess, agree, apply.

421
00:31:59,300 --> 00:32:01,940
This is the biblical practice of repentance.

422
00:32:01,940 --> 00:32:09,960
So, if confession is we say the same thing that God is saying, we believe what he says, then applying or repentance is going in the same direction.

423
00:32:09,960 --> 00:32:15,500
So, it's acknowledging, like, I've been going in a different direction than God has commanded.

424
00:32:15,500 --> 00:32:22,500
I'm going to agree that his way is better than my way, and I'm going to take practical steps in the right direction.

425
00:32:23,600 --> 00:32:31,160
And James here, in this illustration, is he's giving us the framework for how we should view God's word for the rest of our lives.

426
00:32:31,160 --> 00:32:32,300
This is it.

427
00:32:32,300 --> 00:32:35,060
When we're confronted with God's word, this is what we should do.

428
00:32:35,060 --> 00:32:37,940
We should allow it to tell us what is true about ourselves.

429
00:32:37,940 --> 00:32:43,100
We should allow it to tell us when we're not being conformed into the image of Jesus.

430
00:32:43,800 --> 00:32:48,040
We should learn to agree with what God says, even when we don't always like it.

431
00:32:48,040 --> 00:32:49,580
Wrestle with that.

432
00:32:49,580 --> 00:32:50,160
Why is it?

433
00:32:50,160 --> 00:32:52,280
Am I understanding the text rightly?

434
00:32:52,280 --> 00:32:55,920
Like, do I understand what God's asking me to do and why he's asking me to do it?

435
00:32:55,920 --> 00:32:57,780
And if I still don't agree with it, why is that?

436
00:32:57,780 --> 00:33:04,700
And do this in community, because there's value to brothers and sisters in Christ helping you learn to agree with God's word.

437
00:33:05,840 --> 00:33:09,160
And then take practical steps in the right direction.

438
00:33:09,160 --> 00:33:10,060
And then I would say this.

439
00:33:10,060 --> 00:33:14,960
Don't be discouraged when you take two steps forward and one step back, because we're broken.

440
00:33:14,960 --> 00:33:16,680
We're sinners.

441
00:33:16,680 --> 00:33:17,340
We fall short.

442
00:33:17,440 --> 00:33:22,180
And that's the word of truth, that Jesus came and was perfect on our behalf.

443
00:33:22,180 --> 00:33:23,320
We don't have to be perfect.

444
00:33:23,320 --> 00:33:25,360
We just take steps in the right direction.

445
00:33:25,360 --> 00:33:29,780
And when we fall and when we mess up, we give ourselves grace and we give others grace.

446
00:33:29,780 --> 00:33:33,120
And we stand back up and we keep walking in the right direction.

447
00:33:33,120 --> 00:33:34,840
Assess.

448
00:33:34,840 --> 00:33:35,280
Agree.

449
00:33:35,280 --> 00:33:35,980
Apply.

450
00:33:35,980 --> 00:33:36,900
Repeat.

451
00:33:36,900 --> 00:33:44,860
I got to witness this up close and personal a week or two ago in my microchurch.

452
00:33:44,940 --> 00:33:50,760
And if you are not in a microchurch, if you don't have, like, a small group of people, it doesn't have to be sanctioned by canvas.

453
00:33:50,760 --> 00:33:57,320
